`,c.jsx(t.p,{children:"Inside a corporate network, this assumption is completely fine. If you’re Uber, Google, or Stripe, you know precisely which physical servers belong to your data center clusters."}),`
`,c.jsx(t.p,{children:"But a public blockchain can't make that assumption."}),`
`,c.jsx(t.p,{children:"Anyone should be able to join. Anyone should be able to leave. Nobody should need permission from a central entity."}),`
